            "target_entity_type": "SimulationType",
            "paragraph": "The Infoworks ICM model adopted in this study is a 1D-2D coupled hydrodynamic model, a simplified approach from Navier- Stokes Equations, developed by Autodesk. Infoworks ICM can integrate Geographic Information Systems and hydraulic modelling, which is suitable for promoting open spatial data in Hong Kong. A key feature of Inforworks ICM is its ability to model realistic interactions between surface runoff and a 1D underground drainage network across different simulated rainfall scenarios. This software is widely adopted in urban flooding studies, for instance, load tests of the river and stress tests of the drainage system.",
